The review found 10 issues on `2026-09-26-tool-config-gates`. The most serious are:

1. JS repos whose package manager is generated rather than a shipped pack (the bun bundle) lose the `node_modules` allowlist entry, so the full `code:sec` secret scan will fail on them.
2. The new `*.xcassets` exclude fails to cover the files inside an Xcode asset catalog.
3. `code:graph`'s lock can stay held forever if a PID is reused.

Checks run: `vitest run scripts/src/check.test.ts` passed (165 tests) and `mise run p:plugins:check` passed. Nothing was changed.

Stale docs in `CLAUDE.md`, `readme.md`, the site and `.claude/**`, and the unbumped pack versions, are owned by units U10 and U11, which haven't run yet. I reported the docs rule only as a low-severity conventions note (finding 9).

